**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests`

**How to implement.** What a detector records, and each measured point paired with what fixes its prediction (001 §K 'Observables: intensity, Ψ / Δ, full Mueller matrices (the 0044 `MuellerObservation` shape, normalized + absolute throughput). A study mixes them'; step 304: '`ObservationPoints` pass as read, each observation carrying its own configuration, which the study pairs with the experiment (S11.2)'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs`, `module StudyForward` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `PrefitChecks.fs` (step 369), the last Domain file, because the forward model reads studies, setups, items, the evaluator and the data seam: one `<Compile Include="StudyForward.fs" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: the forward model of an experiment and the study residual (spec 0050 S11.2). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In order: (a) `StudyForwardError`, an `*Error` union, its first case `UnpairedPointsErr of reason : string` (a mapped point the experiment's scan cannot place), with `member this.describe : string`: `the data cannot be placed on the scan: <reason>`. Later steps add their cases, each with its line. (b) `RecordedReading` = `RecordedSignal of MeasuredIntensity` (an intensity detector's signal) | `RecordedPsiDelta of PsiDelta` (an ellipsometer's Ψ and Δ, `AnalysisFunctions.fs:PsiDelta`) | `RecordedMueller of MuellerMatrix` (a polarimeter's ABSOLUTE Mueller matrix, its m₀₀ the throughput, as S9.2's Mueller readings hold it, steps 301-302): what a detector records, predicted or measured. (c) `MeasuredRow` = `SettingsRow of settings : ScanSetting list * waveLengthOpt : WaveLength option * measured : RecordedReading` (a point taken at those scan settings, step 287, at its own wavelength when it carries one) | `ObservationRow of observation : MuellerObservation` (a point carrying its own configuration, `MuellerInverse.fs:MuellerObservation`). (d) `type MappedPoints with member this.measuredRowsFor (scan : ExperimentScan) : Result<MeasuredRow list, StudyForwardError>`: the points in their order, each placed by the rules `validatedFor` checks (step 304) over `scan.quantities` (step 304), a quantity set as `{ elementId; variable; value }` with the value `validatedFor` admits for the point, through the same conversion: a `SeriesPoints (IntensityData s)` point is `SettingsRow` of the one quantity at its x, no wavelength, and `RecordedSignal` of its intensity; a `SeriesPoints (EllipsometricData s)` point is `SettingsRow` of the scan's `VaryR2` quantity at its angle of incidence when it carries one and the scan has that quantity (else no setting), `Some` of its wavelength, and `RecordedPsiDelta` of its Ψ and Δ; a `CapturePoints` row is `SettingsRow` of the one quantity at its `description` in degrees, no wavelength, and `RecordedSignal` of its `avgTotal`; a `ColumnPoints` row is `SettingsRow` of the quantities, cell i the i-th quantity at the cell's `displayValue`, no wavelength, and `RecordedSignal` of a `SignalReading`'s signal (its σ is not read: a study weighs runs and detectors, 001 §L) or `RecordedMueller` of a `MuellerReading`; an `ObservationPoints` observation is `ObservationRow` of it. Under a scan of no quantity (a dark line, step 287) a series point, capture row or column row has no setting. A series point or capture row under more than one quantity, and a column row whose cells do not number the quantities, answer `UnpairedPointsErr` naming the point's number and the counts. No cache or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs`, `module StudyForwardTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over test-local scans of `ScanAxis` records on test-local element ids: `each kind of mapped point is placed on the scan it was taken over`: under a one-axis `VaryR1` scan of a polarizer, an intensity series at x 0 and 30 gives two `SettingsRow`s setting the polarizer's `VaryR1` to 0 and 30, no wavelength, their intensities; under a one-axis `VaryDialReading` scan, a capture row of description 20° sets the dial reading to 20 with its `avgTotal`; under a two-axis scan (the polarizer's `VaryR1` outer, a sample's `VaryR2` inner), a column row of cells 10 and 45 sets both in that order, and its `MuellerReading` is `RecordedMueller`; an ellipsometric point at 500 nm with an angle of incidence of 60° under that scan sets the sample's `VaryR2` to 60 with `Some` 500 nm and its Ψ and Δ; observations give one `ObservationRow` each, in order; under a dark-line scan a series point has no setting. `a point the scan cannot place is refused`: under the two-axis scan an intensity series point, a capture row and a column row of one cell each answer `UnpairedPointsErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct payload renders its text with it.

**Acceptance.** After the readings land, `MappedPoints.measuredRowsFor` MUST place every kind of mapped point on its experiment's scan or refuse it with `UnpairedPointsErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `each kind of mapped point is placed on the scan it was taken over`, `a point the scan cannot place is refused` and `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.
